{"title":"Release 2.1.1","type":"release","content":"<!--\nLicensed to the Apache Software Foundation (ASF) under one\nor more contributor license agreements. See the NOTICE file\ndistributed with this work for additional information\nregarding copyright ownership. The ASF licenses this file\nto you under the Apache License, Version 2.0 (the\n\"License\"); you may not use this file except in compliance\nwith the License. You may obtain a copy of the License at\n\n  http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0\n\nUnless required by applicable law or agreed to in writing,\nsoftware distributed under the License is distributed on an\n\"AS IS\" BASIS, WITHOUT WARRANTIES OR CONDITIONS OF ANY\nKIND, either express or implied. See the License for the\nspecific language governing permissions and limitations\nunder the License.\n-->\n\n<p>Apache Paimon 2.1.1 and PyPaimon 2.1.1 include the following fixes on the 2.1 branch.</p>\n<h2 id=\"correctness-and-reliability-fixes\">Correctness and reliability fixes</h2><ul>\n<li>Preserve files reused by compaction when aborting commits (<a href=\"https://github.com/apache/paimon/pull/10582\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"null\" rel=\"noopener\">#10582</a>).</li>\n<li>Delete only tag metadata when deleting tags (<a href=\"https://github.com/apache/paimon/pull/10823\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"null\" rel=\"noopener\">#10823</a>), and disable automatic conflict rollback by default (<a href=\"https://github.com/apache/paimon/pull/10768\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"null\" rel=\"noopener\">#10768</a>).</li>\n<li>Fix Iceberg snapshot summary totals and manifest pruning for removed files (<a href=\"https://github.com/apache/paimon/pull/10575\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"null\" rel=\"noopener\">#10575</a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/apache/paimon/pull/10649\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"null\" rel=\"noopener\">#10649</a>).</li>\n<li>Preserve table UUIDs in REST rollback requests, support branch creation from expired tag snapshots, and align Python rollback behavior with Java (<a href=\"https://github.com/apache/paimon/pull/10528\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"null\" rel=\"noopener\">#10528</a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/apache/paimon/pull/10880\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"null\" rel=\"noopener\">#10880</a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/apache/paimon/pull/10934\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"null\" rel=\"noopener\">#10934</a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/apache/paimon/pull/11049\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"null\" rel=\"noopener\">#11049</a>).</li>\n<li>Fix Data Evolution updates involving rolled vector and BLOB files (<a href=\"https://github.com/apache/paimon/pull/11085\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"null\" rel=\"noopener\">#11085</a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/apache/paimon/pull/11118\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"null\" rel=\"noopener\">#11118</a>).</li>\n<li>Record correct delete row counts and preserve numeric types and explicit JSON nulls during Python VARIANT shredding (<a href=\"https://github.com/apache/paimon/pull/10435\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"null\" rel=\"noopener\">#10435</a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/apache/paimon/pull/10633\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"null\" rel=\"noopener\">#10633</a>).</li>\n<li>Fix Jindo stream lifetime, REST FileIO caching and fork handling, and propagation of unchecked FileIO loader failures (<a href=\"https://github.com/apache/paimon/pull/10536\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"null\" rel=\"noopener\">#10536</a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/apache/paimon/pull/10552\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"null\" rel=\"noopener\">#10552</a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/apache/paimon/pull/10556\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"null\" rel=\"noopener\">#10556</a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/apache/paimon/pull/10752\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"null\" rel=\"noopener\">#10752</a>).</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"dependency-compatibility\">Dependency compatibility</h2><ul>\n<li>Keep release-2.1 Rust wheels below 0.5.0 (<a href=\"https://github.com/apache/paimon/pull/11218\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"null\" rel=\"noopener\">#11218</a>).</li>\n<li>Limit Ray to below 2.60 and cap pyroaring at 1.0.3 on Python 3.8 (<a href=\"https://github.com/apache/paimon/pull/10986\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"null\" rel=\"noopener\">#10986</a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/apache/paimon/pull/10500\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"null\" rel=\"noopener\">#10500</a>).</li>\n<li>Fix readerwriterlock compatibility on Python 3.6/3.7 (<a href=\"https://github.com/apache/paimon/pull/10532\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"null\" rel=\"noopener\">#10532</a>).</li>\n<li>Update Testcontainers for Docker API compatibility and update the approved PyPI publishing action (<a href=\"https://github.com/apache/paimon/pull/10530\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"null\" rel=\"noopener\">#10530</a>, <a href=\"https://github.com/apache/paimon/pull/11223\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"null\" rel=\"noopener\">#11223</a>).</li>\n</ul>\n<p>See the <a href=\"https://github.com/apache/paimon/compare/release-2.1.0...release-2.1.1\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"null\" rel=\"noopener\">2.1.1 changelog</a> for the complete changes since 2.1.0.</p>\n<h2 id=\"downloads-and-packages\">Downloads and Packages</h2><ul>\n<li><a href=\"https://downloads.apache.org/paimon/paimon-2.1.1/\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"null\" rel=\"noopener\">Apache Paimon 2.1.1 source, signature and SHA-512 checksum</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://downloads.apache.org/paimon/pypaimon-2.1.1/\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"null\" rel=\"noopener\">PyPaimon 2.1.1 source, signature and SHA-512 checksum</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://downloads.apache.org/paimon/KEYS\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"null\" rel=\"noopener\">Apache Paimon KEYS for signature verification</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://github.com/apache/paimon/releases/tag/release-2.1.1\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"null\" rel=\"noopener\">Apache Paimon 2.1.1 GitHub release</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://pypi.org/project/pypaimon/2.1.1/\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"null\" rel=\"noopener\">PyPaimon 2.1.1 on PyPI</a></li>\n<li><a href=\"https://paimon.apache.org/docs/2.1/\" target=\"_blank\" title=\"null\" rel=\"noopener\">Apache Paimon 2.1 documentation</a></li>\n</ul>\n<p>Install the Python convenience package with:</p>\n<pre class=\"code\"><code>pip install pypaimon<span class=\"token operator\">==</span><span class=\"token number\">2.1</span><span class=\"token number\">.1</span></code></pre><p>Thank you to every contributor, reviewer and user who helped develop and\nverify this release.</p>\n","toc":[{"depth":2,"text":"Correctness and reliability fixes","id":"correctness-and-reliability-fixes"},{"depth":2,"text":"Dependency compatibility","id":"dependency-compatibility"},{"depth":2,"text":"Downloads and Packages","id":"downloads-and-packages"}],"alias":"release-2.1.1","version":"2.1.1","weight":99}